  "_doc": {
    "about": "How a device paces its Gmail calls (shared/src/gmail-pace.ts, Android :core gmail/GmailPace.kt). Run by shared/src/gmail-pace.spec.ts and Android :core GmailPaceFixturesTest.",
    "usageLimit": "isUsageLimit(status, reason)",
    "backoff": "backoffMs(strike, retryAfterSeconds, jitter) in milliseconds",
    "retry": "retriesAfterLimit(isRead, attempt)",
    "offline": "offlineAfter(offline, event): any answer, even an error status, clears the mark; no answer or the network going shows it; a timeout changes nothing",
    "next": "nextCall(waiting, state, now): the id to start now, or null, and when to look again (wakeAt), or null",
    "saving": "'saving' is a saved-copy read: it yields to every other call, runs at most MAX_SAVING (2) at once, starts SAVING_SPACING_MS (250) after the last one, and waits until savingHeldUntil, which a usage limit sets to SAVING_HOLD_MS (30000) after its pause ends",
    "savingHold": "savingHeldUntil(pausedUntil): when saved-copy reads may go again after a usage limit"
  },
